  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Added:\n- Inline default values for placeholders. Set\n  TemplatedConfigurationOptions.DefaultValueSeparator (conventionally \":-\") to\n  let a placeholder carry its own fallback: {Db:Host:-localhost} resolves to\n  the value of Db:Host when that key has one, and to the literal \"localhost\"\n  when it does not. The first occurrence of the separator splits the\n  placeholder, so a default may itself contain the separator. A default is\n  literal text: an empty default erases the placeholder, and delimiters inside\n  a default are not resolved further. The default is also used when the key\n  resolves to an empty value, whereas a placeholder without a default still\n  substitutes the empty string. A placeholder carrying a default always\n  resolves, so its value is emitted by the provider and it never trips\n  ThrowOnUnresolvedPlaceholders. The separator is unset by default, which\n  leaves placeholder parsing exactly as it was.\n\nFixed:\n- Disposing the provider now releases the configuration root it built even\n  when unsubscribing from the underlying reload token throws, so the sources\n  it opened are no longer leaked on that path.",
